  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 1267250,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "Challenge yourself with 15 Solitaire, a captivating puzzle game for the Commodore 64! This unique solitaire variant presents a board filled with cards, and your objective is to clear them all. The core mechanic revolves around strategically marking cards of the same color whose combined point value equals 15. Successfully marked groups vanish, replaced by fresh cards drawn from a reserve of 36.\n\nHowever, there's a twist! Cards numbered 10, Jack, Queen, and King hold no point value and require all four of the same color to be marked simultaneously for removal. A clever exception allows for a special combination: mark three zero-value cards and a 9, and the 9 will then be treated as a zero-value card, enabling its removal. \n\nMastering this rule is key to conquering the increasingly complex board layouts. With its simple premise and surprisingly deep strategic elements, 15 Solitaire offers hours of engaging gameplay. Originally released on a \"Disk Only\" basis in COMPUTE!'s Gazette, this is a must-have for any Commodore 64 enthusiast seeking a fresh and challenging solitaire experience."
    },
